#X text 660 20 bridge_bufferManager: pure file-system/session-lookup half of buffer_manager.js (see src/max/buffer_manager.js for the un-scoped-down original\, and CONVERSION_NOTES.md "buffer_manager: native-Pd rewrite" for the split rationale). Owns the slotToTrack registry and htdemucs path construction only -- every live buffer~/array operation (src loads\, ring/bake fluid.bufcompose~\, the sync barrier) stays in buffer_manager.pd/buffer_manager_stem.pd/cycle_slot.pd. Inlet 0 takes 3 messages: "sourceTrack <slotIdx> <name...>" (register)\, "resolvePath <sh> <sourceSlot>" (request)\, "resetMemory" (clear the registry). [pd packOSC] -> [netsend -u -b] outbound\, same idiom as every other bridge in this project., f 380;
#X text 660 220 2 outlets: outlet 0 = status (tag + args\, e.g. "registered 1 mytrack"\, "error resolvePath no_name voc 3"\, "cleared") -- wire to a [print] for debugging. outlet 1 = gotPath\, a 3-atom list "<sh> <sourceSlot> <path>" -- wire into buffer_manager_stem.pd\, which turns it into a soundfiler read against src_<sourceSlot>_<sh>-0/-1 (same [soundfiler] pattern as stem_loader.pd)., f 380;
#X text 660 340 Start the bridge alongside Pd: node bridge/buffer_manager_bridge.js --data-dir /path/to/EBYS/data --recv-port 9008 --send-port 9009 (distinct from the other bridges' ports -- streamWatcher=9001\, sliceWriter=9002/9003\, slicer=9004/9005\, analyzeReader=9006/9007 -- so all five can run at once)., f 380;
